WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:05.080
We Can Be Heroes has been an epic success
on Netflix, but many fans have been wondering

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.160
what happened to characters like Max from
the original Sharkboy and Lavagirl movie.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:13.089
And now thanks to some crazy fun fan theories,
we may well have the answer!

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:17.860
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the top seven Sharkboy

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:21.000
and Lavagirl fan theories about We Can Be
Heroes.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.810
Just before we begin, many thanks to the sponsor
of this video, Raid Shadow Legends.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.570
We will, of course, be talking spoilers, so
take care.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:32.880
One of the most popular fan theories is that
Max is actually Miracle Guy.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.160
Given that Sharkboy and Lavagirl are now adults,
it seems plausible that Miracle Guy is what

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.900
Max could grow up to look like.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.140
Which it could also explain how he knows about
the song that Sharkboy sang to Max in the

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.140
original movie.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.770
"Cheer us up by singing one of those songs
you sing so well, Sharkboy?"

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.960
"Close your eyes, shut your mouth.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.810
Dream a dream and get us out."

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:56.010
In fact, Miracle Guy's snarky attitude on
display here could be down to the fact the

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.810
lullaby ended up giving Max nightmares during
his adventure on Planet Drool.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:05.030
Max being Miracle Guy could also explain why
he's one of the most powerful heroes in the

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:09.609
Heroics with a wide range of abilities at
his disposal from flying to super-strength

00:01:09.609 --> 00:01:10.609
and agility.

00:01:10.609 --> 00:01:15.369
Remember that in the Sharkboy and Lavagirl
movie after arriving on Planet Drool, Max

00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:17.609
learned that he also had powers of his own.

00:01:17.609 --> 00:01:18.609
"I have powers?"

00:01:18.609 --> 00:01:19.770
"More than any of us."

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:23.749
In that movie, he was not only able to run
at super speed, but he could also conjure

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:25.799
objects out of thin air.

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:30.520
If We Can Be Heroes is another of Max's dreams,
as some fans have suggested, then it'd make

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.600
sense that he'd give himself an impressive
set of powers, as well as a starring role

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:35.990
in the adult super-team.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:41.149
But even if the film isn't a dream, then Max
may simply have made his dreams of becoming

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:45.689
a powerful superhero come true in the real
world, as suggested in the original movie.

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:49.020
"Some dreams are so powerful, they become
real."

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.130
"So dream a better dream...
then work to make it real."

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.560
One aspect of the theory that doesn't work
so well is how conceited and attention-seeking

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:58.639
Miracle Guy can be.

00:01:58.639 --> 00:02:01.899
"Just a quick selfie for my socials while
I stop this thing."

00:02:01.899 --> 00:02:06.560
And this behaviour doesn't fit Max's personality
when he was younger, however, it is possible

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.349
that as he grew up, his character changed
and he ended up more like Miracle Guy.

00:02:11.349 --> 00:02:15.180
Another theory about Max is that he could
be the father of Ojo, the mysterious young

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.560
girl who turns out to be the Supreme Commander
of Ogima and an alien herself!

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:24.340
After all, in the Sharkboy and Lavagirl movie,
Max draws characters in his dream journal

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:25.680
that come to life.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.040
And likewise, in We Can Be Heroes, Ojo draws
creatures like the Squiggle monsters on her

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.219
tablet and they come alive.

00:02:32.219 --> 00:02:36.560
And could Ojo's ability to see events that
will occur in the future be related to Max's

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:42.241
power to make his dreams come true,
"Everything that is or was, began with a dream."

00:02:42.241 --> 00:02:46.390
in a similar way to how Guppy doesn't have
the exact same powers as her parents, but

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.970
versions of them.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:52.250
Another fan theory that builds on the idea
of Max being Ojo's father is that, after the

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:57.000
events of Sharkboy and Lavagirl, Max became
the ruler of Ogima, the alien planet that

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Ojo is from.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.950
Remember, kids are the ones in charge there.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:04.930
According to this theory, later adult Max
ended up marrying the alien Ms Granada, and

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:08.030
they had an alien daughter together who they
called Ojo.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:12.710
Max then decided to send his wife and child
to Earth disguised as humans to set up the

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.069
plan for the kids of the Heroics to take over
from their parents.

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:20.840
On top of that, this fan theory also suggests
that Max created a clone of himself, in the

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.870
form of Miracle Guy, who he sent to earth
as well.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:28.249
An interesting observation made by "Dylan
Keller" is that the superhero "Mr Positive"

00:03:28.249 --> 00:03:32.650
that Linus was drawing at the end of the Sharkboy
and Lavagirl movie has a similar look to Miracle

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:33.650
Guy.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:38.010
He's got a blue costume and a cape, and although
Mr Positive's logo is different to the 'H'

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:42.650
for Heroics on Miracle Guy's costume, there
does seem to be an overall resemblance in

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:43.739
their look.

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:48.540
It's a curious idea, but could this suggest
that Linus dreamed Miracle Guy into existence?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.569
Some dreams are so powerful they become real.

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:53.519
Perhaps that's how Miracle Guy got some of
his less desirable qualities, such as when

00:03:53.519 --> 00:03:55.870
he tried to pick a fight with Sharkboy.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:04:01.310
Another fun theory comes from "The Hyper Monkey"
who wonders whether Max could be Wild Card's

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.310
father.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:06.230
The idea comes from the fact that Wild Card
has any power he wants at his disposal.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:09.540
"There's not a single power in the world he
doesn't have."

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.999
And his only difficulty is controlling that
ability and so he's never sure what he might

00:04:13.999 --> 00:04:17.350
turn into or what power he might summon.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:18.350
"Teleport!

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.340
Heat vision!"

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:24.320
"Now he's a toaster."

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.250
Max too was able to summon a wide array of
powers when he fought against Minus in the

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:33.230
Sharkboy and Lavagirl film, creating all kinds
of objects from bubbles to butterflies and

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:35.190
even a shower of brains.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:39.750
If this fan theory were true, then we'd have
to assume that Wild Card's father, Tech-No

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.460
was actually the grown-up Max.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:46.531
Although they do look quite different, like
young Max in real life, Tech-No doesn't have

00:04:46.531 --> 00:04:48.340
any super-human abilities.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:53.650
Tech-No is, however, great at building gadgets
and gizmos such as jetpacks, similar perhaps

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:57.980
to Max's talent and interests as a child such
as when he built Tobor.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:03.190
A theory by "tarah 4" is that Marissa, Max's
crush in the Sharkboy and Lavagirl movie,

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:07.360
could be Missy's mother, who's no longer alive
in We Can Be Heroes.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.510
This theory points out that next to Missy's
alarm clock is a picture of her as a baby

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.420
with her mother, and hanging over that is
a necklace,

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:18.570
which makes "tarah 4" think of the magical
necklace that the Ice Princess wore in the

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:19.920
original movie.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.441
Although the necklace on Missy's bedside table
is different to the Crystal Heart, remember

00:05:24.441 --> 00:05:29.290
that Marissa only got her ability to freeze
water and time when she put the Crystal Heart

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:33.110
necklace on;
without it she didn't have any innate superpowers.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:37.140
Which fits Missy and her grandmother's conversation
about her mother not having any superpowers.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.770
"Do you know who the greatest superhero of
them all was?

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.160
It was your mother."

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:44.490
"But my mother was normal, like me."

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.600
What's also intriguing about this theory is
that it implies the necklace on Missy's bedside

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:52.640
table could have magical powers and give her
some kind of special abilities

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:56.580
if she puts it on in the We Can Be Heroes
sequel that's now in development at Netflix.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:01.910
I don't think that will happen but if it did,
I imagine it wouldn't be a major part of Missy's

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:04.310
story
as it would take away from the deliberate

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:08.770
choice writer-director Robert Rodriguez made
for the character without any powers to be

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:11.270
the one "who makes the biggest difference".

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:16.790
Marissa being Missy's mother leads into another
fan theory that Missy's father, Marcus Moreno

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:20.830
is actually Max who ended up with his crush
from the original movie.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:25.220
Remember, Marissa drew a picture of Ice Girl
and Dream Boy together holding hands in the

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.330
first film.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.530
And in the new movie when Missy's grandmother
says

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:34.460
without your mother, your father never would
have become someone who leads by example

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:38.910
could she be referring to how Marissa saved
everyone from the villain Mr Electric when

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.590
he came to the real world?

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:44.920
And perhaps her heroic deed is what inspired
Max to become the leader of the Heroics when

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:45.920
he grew up?

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:50.250
The same way Missy inspires the new Heroics
to bring out the best in themselves.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:54.180
One problem with this fan theory, of course,
is that adult Marcus looks different to what

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:58.790
you'd expect an adult Max to look like,
and while people can certainly be fair-haired

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:03.880
as children and dark-haired as adults that
doesn't change the fact that the filmmaker

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:08.150
cast Latinx actors as both Marcus and Missy
but not Max.

